1
00:00:01,585 --> 00:00:04,296
FRIENDS, FAMILY, WE'RE GATHERED
TO CELEBRATE HERE TODAY

2
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:08,133
THE JOYOUS UNION
OF ROSS AND EMILY.

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:10,928
NOW, ROSS
REPEAT AFTER ME.

4
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:13,722
I, ROSS...
I, ROSS...

5
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:17,351
...TAKE THEE, EMILY...
...TAKE THEE, RACHEL...

6
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:20,646
( screaming )

7
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:22,815
EMILY.

8
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,442
( nervous chuckle ):
EMILY.

9
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,738
UH, SHALL I GO ON?

10
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,157
H-HE SAID RACHEL, RIGHT?

11
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:34,409
DO YOU THINK
I SHOULD GO UP THERE?

12
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,996
YES, YES, DO GO ON.

13
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:39,581
I THINK
WE'D BETTER START AGAIN.

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:42,543
ROSS, REPEAT AFTER ME.

15
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:45,462
I, ROSS...
I, ROSS...

16
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,214
...TAKE THEE, EMILY...

17
00:00:50,718 --> 00:00:52,928
...TAKE THEE, EMILY...

18
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:58,433
IT'S NOT LIKE THERE'D
BE ANYBODY ELSE.

19
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:02,646
...AS MY LAWFULLY WEDDED WIFE,
IN SICKNESS AND IN HEALTH

20
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:04,189
TILL DEATH PARTS US.

21
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,067
...AS MY LAWFULLY
WEDDED WIFE

22
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,444
IN SICKNESS
AND IN HEALTH

23
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:12,239
UNTIL DEATH PARTS US.

24
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:13,741
REALLY, I DO...
( giggle )

25
00:01:13,741 --> 00:01:15,325
...EMILY.

26
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:16,618
DO WE HAVE
THE RINGS?

27
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:21,373
EMILY, PLACE THIS
RING ON ROSS' FINGER

28
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:24,334
AS A SYMBOL OF YOUR
BOND EVERLASTING.

29
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:29,130
AH!

30
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:32,384
ROSS,
PLACE THIS RING

31
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:34,929
ON EMILY'S HAND
AS A SYMBOL

32
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:37,305
OF THE LOVE
THAT ENCIRCLES YOU FOREVER.

33
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:39,182
HAPPY TO.

34
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,520
ROSS AND EMILY
HAVE MADE THEIR DECLARATION

35
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,480
AND IT GIVES ME GREAT PLEASURE

36
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,857
TO DECLARE THEM
HUSBAND AND WIFE.

37
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,362
YOU MAY KISS THE BRIDE.

38
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:59,578
THIS IS WORSE THAN WHEN
HE MARRIED THE LESBIAN.

39
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:06,543
JUST KEEP SMILING.

40
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:08,211
OKAY.

41
00:02:10,464 --> 00:02:13,258
WELL, THAT WENT
WELL. YEAH.

42
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:15,886
COULD HAVE BEEN WORSE.
HE COULD HAVE SHOT HER.

43
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:22,142
( chuckling nervously )
THAT, UH, THAT WAS
PRETTY FUNNY, WASN'T IT?

44
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:24,227
( grunting )

45
00:02:30,109 --> 00:02:34,738
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

46
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:37,032
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

47
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:40,077
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

48
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:44,372
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

49
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:46,959
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

50
00:02:46,959 --> 00:02:49,419
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

51
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:53,298
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

52
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,134
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

53
00:02:55,134 --> 00:02:58,261
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

54
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:00,221
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

55
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:03,308
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

56
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:06,145
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

57
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,737
Emily:
YOU SPOILED EVERYTHING!
IT'S LIKE A NIGHTMARE!

58
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:17,364
MY FRIENDS AND FAMILY
ARE OUT THERE!

59
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,408
HOW CAN I FACE THEM?
HOW COULD YOU DO THIS TO ME?!

60
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,911
HEY, NO MATTER
WHAT HAPPENS WITH
ROSS AND EMILY

61
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:26,581
WE STILL GET
CAKE, RIGHT?

62
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:28,000
T-THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

63
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,584
YOU, NO, NO,
YOU TAKE YOUR TIME, SWEETIE.

64
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,837
I'LL BE RIGHT OUT HERE.

65
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:35,549
( nervous laugh )
SHE'S JUST FIXING HER MAKEUP.

66
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:37,092
Emily:
I HATE YOU!

67
00:03:37,092 --> 00:03:39,887
AND I LOVE YOU!

68
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:44,432
BOY, BAD TIME TO SAY
THE WRONG NAME, HUH, ROSS?

69
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:49,063
THAT'S TRUE.
THANKS, DAD.

70
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:53,232
HEY, PEOPLE
SHOULD BE DANCING, HUH?

71
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:56,361
THIS IS A PARTY!
COME ON!

72
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,613
JOEY, DANCE!

73
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,250
( phone ringing )

74
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,169
YES, WALTHAM INTERIORS.

75
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:14,046
OH, HELLO, THIS
IS ROSS GELLER'S

76
00:04:14,046 --> 00:04:16,924
PERSONAL PHYSICIAN,
DR. FILANGIE.

77
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:19,801
WHO?

78
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:24,139
YEAH. I'VE DISCOVERED
THAT ROSS FORGOT
TO TAKE HIS BRAIN MEDICINE.

79
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:26,767
UM, NOW, WITHOUT IT,
UH, IN THE BRAIN OF ROSS,

80
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:30,562
UH, WOMEN'S NAMES
ARE INTERCHANGEABLE...

81
00:04:30,562 --> 00:04:32,522
THROUGH NO FAULT OF HIS OWN.

82
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:36,110
OH, MY GOD. PHOEBE.

83
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:39,404
NO, NOT PHOEBE.
DR. FILANGIE.

84
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,281
OH, NO, YOU HAVE IT, TOO!

85
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,576
HELLO?
( dial tone )

86
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:53,127
HEY.
HEY.

87
00:04:53,127 --> 00:04:56,588
OH, WOW, I HOPE YOU DON'T
TAKE THIS THE WRONG WAY, BUT

88
00:04:56,588 --> 00:05:00,008
I KNOW WE HAD PLANS
TO MEET UP TONIGHT, AND...

89
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,136
AH, I'M JUST,
I'M KIND OF WORRIED

90
00:05:02,136 --> 00:05:04,304
ABOUT WHAT IT MIGHT DO
TO OUR FRIENDSHIP.

91
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,056
I KNOW.

92
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:07,808
OH, HOW COULD WE
HAVE LET THIS HAPPEN?

93
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,768
SEVEN TIMES!

94
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:15,149
WELL, YOU KNOW,
LOOK, WE WERE AWAY.

95
00:05:15,149 --> 00:05:18,610
IN A FOREIGN,
ROMANTIC COUNTRY.

96
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,903
I BLAME LONDON.

97
00:05:19,903 --> 00:05:21,529
BAD LONDON!

98
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:26,701
SO, LOOK, UM WHILE
WE'RE STILL IN LONDON,

99
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,578
I MEAN, WE CAN KEEP
DOING IT, RIGHT?

100
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:31,748
WELL, I DON'T SEE
THAT WE HAVE A CHOICE.
NO.

101
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:34,417
BUT WHEN WE'RE BACK
HOME, WE DON'T DO IT.

102
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:37,462
ONLY HERE.

103
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:40,048
YOU KNOW, I SAW A
WINE CELLAR DOWNSTAIRS.

104
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,967
MEET YOU THERE
IN TWO MINUTES.
'KAY.

105
00:05:45,512 --> 00:05:47,388
MON, HONEY,
I GOT TO ASK YOU SOMETHING.

106
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:48,515
NOW?

107
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:50,433
ROSS SAID MY NAME UP THERE.

108
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,060
I MEAN, COME ON,
I CAN'T JUST PRETEND

109
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,980
THAT DIDN'T HAPPEN, CAN I?
OH, I-I DON'T KNOW.

110
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,858
MONICA, WHAT SHOULD I DO?
JUST, UH...

111
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,359
DO THE RIGHT THING.

112
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:02,737
WHAT?

113
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:04,363
TOE THE LINE.
THREAD THE NEEDLE.

114
00:06:04,363 --> 00:06:05,782
THINK OUTSIDE THE BOX.

115
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,408
MONICA, WAIT.
I THINK I'M JUST GONNA

116
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:09,368
TALK TO ROSS ABOUT
WHAT HE THINKS IT MEANT.

117
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:12,164
WAIT. RACHEL, NO.

118
00:06:12,164 --> 00:06:14,916
HE'S MARRIED.
MARRIED.

119
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,336
IF YOU DON'T REALIZE THAT,
I CAN'T HELP YOU.

120
00:06:17,336 --> 00:06:20,297
OKAY. YOU'RE RIGHT.

121
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:22,841
YOU'RE RIGHT.
YOU CAN'T HELP ME.

122
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:27,179
JACK, IS IT ALL OUR FAULT?

123
00:06:27,179 --> 00:06:30,265
WERE WE BAD PARENTS?
YES.

124
00:06:30,265 --> 00:06:32,017
OH, YEAH? WELL,
WHO SERVES STEAK

125
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:33,601
WHEN THERE'S NO
PLACE TO SIT?

126
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:35,312
I MEAN, HOW ARE
YOU SUPPOSED
TO EAT THIS?

127
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:38,606
HEY, WHAT'S UP?

128
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:41,151
WHERE WERE YOU?
WE WERE SUPPOSED TO MEET
IN THE WINE CELLAR.

129
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:43,195
FORGET IT.
THAT'S OFF.
WHY?

130
00:06:43,195 --> 00:06:46,447
( drunkenly ):
THE NEXT TOUR OF
THE WINE CELLAR

131
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:50,535
WILL COMMENCE
IN TWO MI-I-INUTES.

132
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:55,082
JOEY, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?
YOU PROMISED PHOEBE

133
00:06:55,082 --> 00:06:56,666
YOU WOULDN'T EAT MEAT
UNTIL SHE HAS THE BABIES.

134
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,335
OH, I FIGURED
WE'RE IN ANOTHER COUNTRY

135
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:00,461
SO IT DOESN'T COUNT.

136
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,172
WELL, THAT'S TRUE.
THE MAN'S GOT A POINT.

137
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,634
OH, HI.

138
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,136
HI.
HI.

139
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:09,971
I'M SORRY THINGS
AREN'T WORKING OUT SO WELL.

140
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,932
OH, NO!
( nervous chuckle ) 

141
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:13,516
COULD BE BETTER.

142
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:16,103
IT'S GONNA
BE OKAY, RIGHT?
OH, YEAH, OF COURSE.

143
00:07:16,103 --> 00:07:17,645
I MEAN, SHE'S GONNA
GET OVER THIS, YOU KNOW?

144
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:19,438
I MEAN,
SO YOU SAID MY NAME.

145
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:22,276
YOU KNOW, YOU JUST SAID IT
'CAUSE YOU SAW ME THERE.

146
00:07:22,276 --> 00:07:23,902
IF YOU'D SEEN
A CIRCUS FREAK

147
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:27,989
YOU WOULD'VE SAID,
"I TAKE THEE, CIRCUS FREAK."

148
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:31,410
YOU KNOW,
IT DIDN'T MEAN ANYTHING.
IT'S JUST A MISTAKE.

149
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:33,453
DIDN'T MEAN ANYTHING.

150
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,955
RIGHT?

151
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:38,041
OH, NO, OF COURSE
IT DIDN'T MEAN ANYTHING.

152
00:07:38,041 --> 00:07:40,335
I MEAN, WHA... I CAN
UNDERSTAND WHY EMILY

153
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:42,045
WOULD THINK IT
MEANT SOMETHING

154
00:07:42,045 --> 00:07:45,632
YOU KNOW, BECAUSE IT WAS YOU,
BUT IT ABSOLUTELY DIDN'T.

155
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:47,426
IT DIDN'T! IT DIDN'T!

156
00:07:49,052 --> 00:07:50,804
ROSS! HEY,
THE BAND'S READY OUTSIDE

157
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:52,347
FOR YOUR FIRST DANCE
WITH EMILY, SO...

158
00:07:52,347 --> 00:07:54,933
OH! OH!
THE BAND'S READY!

159
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:58,145
WELL, WE'VE GOT TO DO
WHAT THE BAND SAYS, RIGHT?

160
00:07:58,145 --> 00:07:59,854
I DON'T CARE ABOUT
THE STUPID BAND!

161
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,524
YOU SPIT ON ME, MAN.

162
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:06,736
I-I'M SORRY.

163
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,948
EMILY IS TAKING
KIND OF A LONG TIME, HUH?

164
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,450
YOU KNOW, WHEN I LOCKED MYSELF
IN THE BATHROOM AT MY WEDDING

165
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:12,993
IT WAS BECAUSE
I WAS TRYING

166
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:15,870
TO POP THE WINDOW
OUT OF THE FRAME,
OH, RIGHT.

167
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,914
AND GET THE HELL
OUT OF THERE, YOU KNOW?

168
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:19,540
( chuckling nervously )

169
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:24,545
EMILY?

170
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,714
EMILY?!

171
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,383
I'M COMING IN!

172
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:32,804
WELL, LOOK AT THAT.
SAME THING.

173
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,060
LISTEN, IN THE MIDDLE
OF EVERYTHING

174
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,438
IF I SCREAM THE WORD "YIPPEE,"
JUST IGNORE ME.

175
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,693
( gasping )
OH, MY GOD, RACHEL! HI.

176
00:08:46,693 --> 00:08:48,278
OH, HELLO, RACHEL.

177
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:51,698
ROSS SAID MY NAME.

178
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,616
OKAY? MY NAME.

179
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,118
ROSS SAID MY
NAME UP THERE.

180
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:58,955
THAT OBVIOUSLY MEANS
THAT HE STILL LOVES ME.

181
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:01,124
OKAY, DON'T BELIEVE ME.
I KNOW I'M RIGHT.

182
00:09:01,124 --> 00:09:03,584
DO YOU GUYS WANT TO GO
DOWNSTAIRS AND GET A DRINK?

183
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,505
YES, WE DO.

184
00:09:06,505 --> 00:09:08,756
BUT WE HAVE
TO CHANGE FIRST.

185
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:11,550
YES, I WANT TO CHANGE.

186
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,387
W-WHY DON'T YOU GO DOWN
AND GET US A TABLE?

187
00:09:13,387 --> 00:09:14,721
YEAH, WE'LL BE DOWN
IN, LIKE, FIVE MINUTES.

188
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:16,723
15 MINUTES.

189
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:18,766
OKAY.

190
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:20,810
( phone ringing )

191
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,604
HELLO. OH, PHEEBS!
IT'S PHOEBE.

192
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,607
( mumbling politely )
HI!

193
00:09:26,607 --> 00:09:28,276
SO, WHAT HAPPENED?

194
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:30,695
WELL, ROSS SAID MY NAME.

195
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:33,156
YEAH, I KNOW, BUT I DON'T THINK
THAT MEANS ANYTHING.

196
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:35,242
OKAY, PHEEBS, YOU KNOW WHAT?
LET'S LOOK AT THIS OBJECTIVELY.

197
00:09:35,242 --> 00:09:37,452
ALL RIGHT, NINTH GRADE, RIGHT?

198
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:40,372
THE OBSESSION STARTS.

199
00:09:40,372 --> 00:09:42,290
ALL RIGHT? SUMMER
AFTER NINTH GRADE

200
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,167
HE SEES ME IN A TWO-PIECE
FOR THE FIRST TIME.

201
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:47,254
HIS OBSESSION BEGINS TO GROW,
RIGHT? SO, THEN...

202
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:49,130
HEY, LISTEN, WHY DON'T
WE GO CHANGE IN MY ROOM?

203
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:52,509
MY CLOTHES ARE... OH!
( chuckling )

204
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:08,066
WOW, YOU LOOK...

205
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:10,360
NO TIME FOR THAT.
OKAY.

206
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:16,116
HEY, DUDE, LET ME IN.
I GOT A GIRL OUT HERE.

207
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:21,246
WELL, I'VE GOT
A GIRL IN HERE.

208
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:23,873
NO, YOU DON'T.
I JUST SAW YOU GO
IN THERE WITH MONICA.

209
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:29,087
WELL, WE'RE
HANGING OUT IN HERE.

210
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:31,714
WHICH ONE OF US IS GOING TO BE
HAVING SEX IN THERE, ME OR YOU?

211
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:36,928
WELL, I SUPPOSE
I WOULD HAVE TO SAY YOU.

212
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:40,098
LOOK, WHAT IF WE'RE WATCHING
A MOVIE IN HERE?

213
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:43,017
W-WHICH WE ARE.
A-AND WE ALREADY PAID FOR IT.

214
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:45,979
IT'S MY GIANT.

215
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:49,774
MY GIANT?
I LOVE THAT MOVIE!

216
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:55,947
YOU REALLY THINK
THIS IS OKAY?

217
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:57,782
WELL, ROSS AND EMILY
AREN'T GOING TO USE IT.

218
00:10:59,159 --> 00:11:01,744
OH, IT'S SO BEAUTIFUL!

219
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,497
OH!

220
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:04,998
YOU KNOW, I DON'T KNOW
IF I FEEL RIGHT ABOUT THIS.

221
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:08,168
OH, M-MON, MON, M-M-MONICA...

222
00:11:08,168 --> 00:11:10,128
THIS IS THE HONEYMOON SUITE.

223
00:11:10,128 --> 00:11:12,422
THE ROOM EXPECTS SEX.

224
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:18,261
THE ROOM WOULD BE DISAPPOINTED
IF IT DIDN'T GET SEX.

225
00:11:18,261 --> 00:11:21,306
ALL OF THE OTHER
HONEYMOON SUITES WOULD
THINK IT WAS A LOSER.

226
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:24,725
OKAY.
OKAY.

227
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:28,062
EMILY?

228
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:30,023
NOPE, NOT UNDER HERE.

229
00:11:32,651 --> 00:11:33,818
YOU DIDN'T FIND HER?

230
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:35,362
NO. I'VE LOOKED EVERYWHERE.

231
00:11:35,362 --> 00:11:37,113
YOU COULDN'T HAVE LOOKED
EVERYWHERE

232
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:38,365
OR ELSE
YOU WOULD'VE FOUND HER.

233
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:39,407
I THINK YOU SHOULD
KEEP LOOKING.

234
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,242
YEAH, FOR ABOUT, UH, 30 MINUTES.

235
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:43,203
OR 45?

236
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:48,166
WOW, IN 45 MINUTES,
YOU COULD FIND HER TWICE.

237
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,881
NO. FOR ALL I KNOW,
SHE'S TRYING TO FIND ME,
BUT COULDN'T

238
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:57,050
BECAUSE I KEPT
MOVING AROUND.

239
00:11:57,050 --> 00:12:00,178
NO, FROM NOW ON,
I'M STAYING IN ONE PLACE.

240
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:02,389
RIGHT HERE.

241
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,310
WELL, IT'S GETTING LATE.
YEAH, WE'RE GOING TO G--

242
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:11,772
YOU GUYS MIND
STAYING HERE FOR A WHILE?

243
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:14,442
YOU KNOW, UM,
WE GOT TO GET UP EARLY

244
00:12:14,442 --> 00:12:15,776
AND CATCH THAT PLANE
TO NEW YORK.

245
00:12:15,776 --> 00:12:17,736
YEAH, IT'S A
VERY LARGE PLANE.

246
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,450
THAT'S COOL.

247
00:12:24,536 --> 00:12:26,287
BUT WE'LL STAY HERE
WITH YOU.

248
00:12:27,372 --> 00:12:28,831
THANKS, GUYS!

249
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,877
I REALLY APPRECIATE THIS,
YOU KNOW?

250
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:34,753
BUT YOU DON'T NEED
TO RUB MY BUTT.

251
00:12:47,726 --> 00:12:50,270
WE HAVE TO LEAVE
FOR NEW YORK IN AN HOUR.

252
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,022
I KNOW. I'VE BEEN
LOOKING AT THOSE DOORS.

253
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,983
THEY LOOK SOUNDPROOF,
DON'T YOU THINK?

254
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:59,028
WE CAN'T DO THAT.
THAT'S INSANE.

255
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:01,030
I MEAN, A: HE COULD WAKE UP.

256
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:03,782
AND B: YOU KNOW...
LET'S GO FOR IT.

257
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:09,038
( knocking on door )

258
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:11,082
EMIL... EMILY?
EM... EMILY!

259
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:17,255
EMILY!
NO.

260
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:19,006
YOU CAN FORGET ABOUT EMILY,
SHE'S NOT WITH US.

261
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:20,133
WE'VE COME FOR
HER THINGS.

262
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,176
W-WHERE IS SHE?

263
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:24,763
SHE'S IN HIDING.
SHE'S UTTERLY HUMILIATED.

264
00:13:24,763 --> 00:13:26,723
SHE DOESN'T WANT
TO SEE YOU EVER AGAIN.

265
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:30,809
WE'RE VERY SAD THAT
IT DIDN'T WORK OUT
BETWEEN YOU AND EMILY...

266
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:33,354
MONKEY.

267
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:38,276
BUT I THINK YOU'RE
ABSOLUTELY DELICIOUS.

268
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:41,946
EXCUSE ME. I'M
STANDING RIGHT HERE.

269
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,949
OH, YES.

270
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:46,867
THERE YOU ARE.

271
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,789
HEY! HEY, YOU GUYS!
GO HURRY UP, GET SOME.

272
00:13:50,789 --> 00:13:52,791
THERE'S A WHOLE CART OUTSIDE.

273
00:13:52,791 --> 00:13:56,210
BYE, GELLER.
WAIT, HOLD ON. HOLD ON.

274
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,338
LOOK, LOOK...
YOUR DAUGHTER AND I

275
00:13:58,338 --> 00:14:00,632
ARE SUPPOSED TO LEAVE
TONIGHT FOR OUR HONEYMOON.

276
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:03,842
NOW... NOW YOU TELL HER
THAT I'M GOING TO BE
AT THAT AIRPORT

277
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:06,387
AND I HOPE THAT
SHE'LL BE THERE, TOO.

278
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,888
OH, YEAH, I SAID
RACHEL'S NAME

279
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:09,223
BUT IT DIDN'T MEAN
ANYTHING, OKAY?

280
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,933
SHE'S JUST A FRIEND.
THAT'S ALL.

281
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:13,186
NOW, LOOK, JUST TELL
EMILY THAT I LOVE HER

282
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:14,729
AND THAT I CAN'T IMAGINE

283
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:16,481
SPENDING MY LIFE
WITH ANYONE ELSE.

284
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:20,109
PLEASE, PROMISE ME THAT
YOU'LL TELL HER THAT.

285
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:23,863
ALL RIGHT. I'LL TELL HER.

286
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:26,282
COME ON, BUGGERFACE.

287
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,618
CALL ME.
( gasps )

288
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:30,328
YOU SPEND HALF YOUR
LIFE IN THE BATHROOM.

289
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:32,747
WHY DO YOU NEVER GO
OUT THE BLOODY WINDOW?

290
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:54,394
YOU KNOW, MAYBE IT'S BEST
WE NEVER GOT TO DO IT AGAIN.

291
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:56,730
YEAH, IT KIND OF MAKES
THAT ONE NIGHT SPECIAL.

292
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:04,738
YOU KNOW, TECHNICALLY
WE STILL ARE OVER
INTERNATIONAL WATERS.

293
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,699
I'M GOING TO GO
TO THE BATHROOM.

294
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:09,826
MAYBE I'LL SEE YOU
THERE IN A BIT?
OKAY.

295
00:15:17,375 --> 00:15:18,959
HEY, CAN I ASK
YOU SOMETHING?

296
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,837
UH... NO.

297
00:15:22,714 --> 00:15:25,258
FELICITY AND I, WE'RE
WATCHING MY GIANT, RIGHT?

298
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:27,926
AND I WAS THINKING,
I'M NEVER GOING TO BE

299
00:15:27,926 --> 00:15:29,888
AS GOOD AN ACTOR
AS THAT GIANT.

300
00:15:29,888 --> 00:15:32,014
DO YOU THINK I'M
JUST WASTING MY LIFE

301
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:33,933
WITH THIS ACTING THING?

302
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,310
NO.

303
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,646
THE GIANT'S, LIKE,
FIVE YEARS YOUNGER
THAN ME, YOU KNOW?

304
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:41,940
YOU THINK I'LL
EVER GET THERE?

305
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:44,151
YES.

306
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:47,822
THANKS, MAN.
OKAY, MAN.

307
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:51,659
BUT WHAT ABOUT HOW MUCH
TALLER HE IS THAN ME?

308
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:55,246
I MEAN, THERE'S
NO WAY I CAN MAKE
MYSELF TALLER NOW.

309
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:58,207
YOU KNOW? AND WHO KNOWS
WHAT SCIENCE WILL COME UP
WITH IN THE FUTURE?

310
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,959
BUT, CHANDLER,
WHAT IF I DIE

311
00:16:00,959 --> 00:16:03,421
AN UNSUCCESSFUL,
REGULAR-SIZE MAN?

312
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:08,426
HEY, MONICA. YOU BEEN
IN THE BATHROOM FOR,
LIKE, A HALF HOUR.

313
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:11,846
I KNOW.

314
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:14,181
HAD THE BEEF TIPS, HUH?

315
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:24,150
( giggles )

316
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,487
HEY!
HEY!
HI!

317
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:32,492
( laughing )
YOU ATE MEAT.

318
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:35,912
YOU HAD SEX!

319
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,373
NO, WE DIDN'T.

320
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,584
I KNOW YOU DIDN'T.
I WAS TALKING ABOUT MONICA.

321
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:45,672
PHOEBE, I DID
NOT HAVE SEX.

322
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:48,758
OH, THIS PREGNANCY IS
THROWING ME ALL OFF.

323
00:16:48,758 --> 00:16:51,010
I'M GONNA GO SAY HI
TO THE CHICK AND THE DUCK.

324
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,304
OH, ME, TOO.
WHY WOULD YOU NEED
TO SAY HI TO THEM?

325
00:16:53,304 --> 00:16:54,973
YOU'VE BEEN FEEDING THEM
FOR FOUR DAYS.

326
00:16:54,973 --> 00:16:57,266
OH, RIGHT. MAYBE
I'LL JUST GO HOME.

327
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:10,446
WELL, WE CERTAINLY
ARE ALONE.

328
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:12,740
YES, GOOD THING WE HAD
THAT "NOT IN NEW YORK" RULE.

329
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,075
RIGHT.

330
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:18,371
UM, LISTEN, SINCE
WE'RE ON THAT SUBJECT...

331
00:17:18,371 --> 00:17:21,499
I JUST WANTED
TO TELL YOU THAT, UM,

332
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:24,042
WELL... I WAS GOING THROUGH
A REALLY HARD TIME IN LONDON

333
00:17:24,042 --> 00:17:26,004
WHAT WITH MY BROTHER
GETTING MARRIED

334
00:17:26,004 --> 00:17:27,964
AND THAT GUY THINKING
I WAS ROSS'S MOTHER.

335
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,591
RIGHT.

336
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:33,427
WELL, ANYWAY, I JUST...

337
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:34,846
THAT NIGHT MEANT
A LOT TO ME

338
00:17:34,846 --> 00:17:37,056
AND I GUESS I'M TRYING
TO SAY THANKS.

339
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,058
OH.

340
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:44,062
YOU KNOW, THAT NIGHT MEANT
A LOT TO ME, TOO.

341
00:17:44,062 --> 00:17:46,315
AND IT WASN'T 'CAUSE I WAS
IN A BAD PLACE OR ANYTHING.

342
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:48,317
IT JUST MEANT A LOT TO ME

343
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:50,611
'CAUSE... YOU'RE REALLY HOT.

344
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:56,116
IS THAT OKAY?

345
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:58,828
THAT'S OKAY.

346
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:00,413
AND I'M CUTE, TOO.

347
00:18:02,373 --> 00:18:03,457
AND YOU'RE CUTE, TOO.

348
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,501
THANK YOU.

349
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:08,046
ALL RIGHT.
I'VE GOT TO GO UNPACK.
OKAY.

350
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,801
BYE.

351
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:28,190
I'M STILL ON LONDON TIME.
DOES THAT COUNT?

352
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:31,819
OH, THAT COUNTS.
OH, GOOD.

353
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,288
RACH!
RACH!

354
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:43,706
HI.

355
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:45,666
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

356
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:49,045
WELL, I'VE BEEN ON STANDBY
FOR A FLIGHT HOME FOR HOURS.

357
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:50,129
OH.

358
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:52,130
OH... SO NO SIGN
OF EMILY, HUH?

359
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:54,133
NOT YET.

360
00:18:56,677 --> 00:19:00,974
SO, UM, WHAT TIME ARE YOU
SUPPOSED TO LEAVE?

361
00:19:00,974 --> 00:19:05,269
P.A.:
This is the last call
for flight 1066 to Athens.

362
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,063
The last call.

363
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:09,107
PRETTY SOON, I GUESS.
YEAH.

364
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:13,527
I'M SORRY.

365
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,321
I JUST... I DON'T
UNDERSTAND.

366
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:20,158
I MEAN, HOW COULD SHE DO THIS?
AM I, LIKE, A COMPLETE IDIOT

367
00:19:20,158 --> 00:19:22,662
FOR THINKING SHE'D
ACTUALLY SHOW UP?

368
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:26,124
NO, YOU'RE NOT AN IDIOT, ROSS.

369
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:28,584
YOU'RE A GUY VERY MUCH IN LOVE.

370
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,210
SAME DIFFERENCE.

371
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:34,256
All ticketed passengers
for flight 1066 to Athens

372
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,842
should now be on board.

373
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,344
I GET IT!

374
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,182
WELL, THAT'S THAT.

375
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,144
NO, YOU KNOW WHAT?

376
00:19:46,144 --> 00:19:48,228
I THINK YOU SHOULD GO.

377
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:50,230
WHAT?
YEAH, I DO.

378
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,191
I THINK YOU SHOULD GO
BY YOURSELF.

379
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,693
GET SOME DISTANCE.

380
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:54,986
CLEAR YOUR HEAD.

381
00:19:54,986 --> 00:19:56,654
I THINK IT WOULD BE
REALLY GOOD.

382
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:59,032
OH, I DON'T, I DON'T KNOW.
OH, COME ON, ROSS.

383
00:19:59,032 --> 00:20:01,742
I THINK IT WOULD BE
REALLY GOOD FOR YOU.

384
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:05,412
I... I... I COULD.
I-I COULD DO THAT.

385
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:07,247
YEAH.

386
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:09,416
I CAN'T EVEN BELIEVE HER.

387
00:20:09,416 --> 00:20:11,919
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I AM GOING TO GO.

388
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:13,171
GOOD.
WHY NOT?

389
00:20:13,171 --> 00:20:15,255
RIGHT!
RIGHT?

390
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:17,967
THANKS.
OKAY, I'LL SEE YOU
BACK AT HOME...

391
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,094
IF I EVER GET A FLIGHT.

392
00:20:20,094 --> 00:20:22,638
HEY, WH... NAH.

393
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:24,640
WHAT? WAIT. WHAT?

394
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,310
WHY DON'T YOU COME?

395
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:32,356
I MEAN, I HAVE TWO TICKETS.
WHY NOT?

396
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:35,943
( mumbling ):
WELL, ROSS, I...

397
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:38,029
REALLY?

398
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:39,321
YEAH, YEAH, IT'D BE GREAT.

399
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:41,782
I MEAN, YOU CAN
LAY ON THE BEACH

400
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:46,037
AND I CAN CRY OVER
MY FAILED MARRIAGE.

401
00:20:46,037 --> 00:20:47,830
SEE HOW I MAKE JOKES?

402
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,331
UH-HUH.

403
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,958
NO, REALLY, I MEAN...

404
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:53,419
GOD, I COULD USE A FRIEND.

405
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:57,215
OH, WOW, OKAY... UH, MAYBE.

406
00:20:57,215 --> 00:20:58,925
UM...

407
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:00,259
YES, I CAN DO THAT.

408
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,635
OKAY, COOL.
COME ON.

409
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:02,720
ALL RIGHT, COOL.

410
00:21:04,931 --> 00:21:06,766
OKAY, WE'RE GOING
TO GREECE.

411
00:21:06,766 --> 00:21:10,144
AH! I FORGOT MY JACKET.

412
00:21:10,144 --> 00:21:11,395
TELL THEM TO WAIT.

413
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:14,648
Rachel:
WAIT! WAIT!

414
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:21,239
EMILY.

415
00:21:25,034 --> 00:21:26,744
OH, NO, NO, NO.

416
00:21:26,744 --> 00:21:28,370
NO, NO...

417
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:30,831
NO! NO!

418
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:32,291
EMILY!

419
00:21:35,293 --> 00:21:38,214
UH, YES, I WILL HAVE
A GLASS OF THE MERLOT,

420
00:21:38,214 --> 00:21:40,800
AND HE WILL HAVE A
WHITE WINE SPRITZER.

421
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:45,930
WHOO.

422
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,807
( chuckling )

423
00:21:47,807 --> 00:21:50,935
HEY, LOOK AT THAT,
THE AIRPORT'S MOVING.

424
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:52,853
HEY, ARE WE MOVING?

425
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:53,854
ARE WE MOVING?

426
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:54,981
WHY ARE WE MOVING?

427
00:21:54,981 --> 00:21:56,649
THAT DOESN'T...

428
00:21:56,649 --> 00:21:59,110
UM, YEAH, DOES THE CAPTAIN KNOW
THAT WE'RE MOVING?

429
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:00,653
OH, MY GOD.

430
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:02,155
OH, MY GOSH.

